      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Proving infringement often requires demonstrating substantial similarity in non-functional aspects or a \"copy-paste\" feeling, rather than just a shared function signature. The client's burden of proof is high to convince a court that your code is an unauthorized copy rather than an independently developed application of general industry knowledge. Ultimately, excellent documentation and keeping distinct separation between projects are your best defenses in such a gray area.",
